This finite catalog expands selected retained names and cited functional-class
rules into complete names. Some resource tokens are stems, not complete names.
The accompanying independent authored graphs and strict parser checks validate
those expansions. This selection does not modify the upstream resources and
is not a complete copy of OPSIN's retained-name vocabulary.

The exact (+)-lactic acid / S-lactic acid equivalence and its molecular graph
are selected from ChEBI:422, EMBL-EBI, last modified 18 April 2024:
https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI:422
Accessed 11 October 2026. ChEBI attributes the (+)-lactic acid synonym to NIST.
This is a finite local adaptation of that record, not a database download or
a general inference from optical rotation signs to absolute configuration.

